    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="81" width="500" height="120" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">IAPWS-IF97 Water and Steam Properties Plugin for SMath Studio</p>
    <p bold="true">Industrial Formulation 1997 for General &amp; Scientific Power-Plant Calculations</p>
    <p bold="true">Native Assembly: IF97Wrapper.dll (Plugin GUID: bdb8d1d9-11bf-4f8b-aca4-c1fa3f6e13ad, v1.1.1.0)</p>
    <p bold="true">Strict SI Unit Guarantee: Pressures in [Pa], Temperatures in [K], Energies in [J/kg] (m^2/s^2), Entropies in [J/(kg*K)]</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="213" width="500" height="360" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">The International Association for the Properties of Water and Steam (IAPWS) IF97 formulation</p>
    <p bold="false">is the international industrial standard for calculating thermodynamic and transport properties</p>
    <p bold="false">of water and steam across power plant engineering, turbomachinery design, and thermal processes.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Key Architectural Highlights of the IF97 SMath Plugin (v1.1.1.0 .NET 2.0 CLR):</p>
    <p bold="false">  1. Pure SI Units: Eliminates unit conversion pitfalls. All inputs accept standard SMath SI units</p>
    <p bold="false">     or bare numbers (implicitly SI); all outputs return strictly in standard SMath SI units.</p>
    <p bold="false">  2. Direct Fast Forward Functions: Sub-microsecond evaluation of h, s, u, rho, v, cp, cv, w, mu, tc, Pr.</p>
    <p bold="false">     Standard argument order is (T, p) with temperature in [K] and pressure in [Pa].</p>
    <p bold="false">  3. Direct Backward Functions: Analytical backward equations T(p,h), rho(p,h), T(p,s), rho(p,s), p(h,s), T(h,s).</p>
    <p bold="false">  4. Wet Steam Two-Phase Region: Saturated liquid/vapor lines, latent heat hfg, and two-phase mixtures.</p>
    <p bold="false">  5. Standardized 46-Function API: Clean IF97_&lt;property&gt;_&lt;inputs&gt; nomenclature with strict base SI unit emission.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="585" width="500" height="56" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">Section 1: Atmospheric &amp; Saturation Boundary Calculations</p>
    <p bold="true">Verification of saturation temperature, saturation pressure, surface tension, and saturated liquid/vapor lines.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="653" width="60" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
